ff802-ucm-profile (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * No change of the UCM files or the binding.
  * README.Debian: behaviour in PipeWire 1.6 / WirePlumber 0.5 (T3
    container test pw_integration): six sinks and one source through
    WirePlumber's own SplitPCM support, no PipeWire/WirePlumber
    configuration needed; new sinks start at 40 % (-23.9 dB); stored
    WirePlumber state overrides that; what removal does not touch.
  * Analog outputs 1 and 2 physically confirmed (T2, partial).

 -- Bernhard Steinheber <bernhard@steinheber.info>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0100

ff802-ucm-profile (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First package of the Fireface 802 UCM profile (CC mode): six stereo
    outputs and one stereo input through UCM SplitPCM.
  * Device binding by card long name (ff802-ucm-bind) as workaround for
    alsa-lib < 1.2.16, which ignores USB-Audio/conf.d.
  * Profile evaluated with the real card (host test T1, 29/29 checks).
    Physical channel assignment not yet verified (hardware test T2).

 -- Bernhard Steinheber <bernhard@steinheber.info>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
